     "label": "Jan 2025 second term",
     "note": "The story begins when Trump returns to office and starts describing Beijing as a co-equal great power rather than a rival to be contained. Under this opening, the current G7 friction, NATO spending demands and outreach to Pyongyang read as one continuous reset built around that reframe. This is the frame Trump-aligned outlets and the White House itself open with."
    },
    {
     "label": "2018 tariff round",
     "note": "The story begins with the Section 301 tariffs and the formal turn to strategic competition with China. Under this opening, today's peer-power language is the latest move inside an eight-year confrontation that the first Trump term started and Biden largely kept. This is the frame China hawks, US trade officials and most Taipei-based coverage open with."
    },
    {
     "label": "1972 Nixon opening",
     "note": "The story begins with Nixon's trip to Beijing and the long bet that engagement would shape Chinese behavior. Under this opening, the current reframing is one more swing in a fifty-year cycle of opening, integration and pullback between two powers that have always managed each other as peers in practice. This is the frame realist historians, Russian and Chinese state outlets and many European analysts open with."
    }
